course: dictionary
lesson: 5114
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one is meant. Intolerance is one of these words. «Lactose intolerance means the body cannot digest milk sugar well.» The clues are «body» and «milk sugar», so this meaning is about food and health.
explain: Intolerance can also mean not being willing to accept people whose ideas, beliefs or ways of life are different from yours. Lessons on citizenship and religious education use it this way, as the opposite of tolerance and respect. The clue in «religious intolerance» is the word religious, which points to people and beliefs.
explain: The third meaning is not being able to bear something, such as heat, cold or pain. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «He had an intolerance of cold» means he could not bear the cold, so the meaning fits.
explain: Watch the phrase too. The correct phrase is «zero tolerance», not zero intolerance. When you are unsure which meaning is right, read the whole sentence again and ask which meaning would make sense there.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Intolerance» has three meanings: not accepting people who are different, a body that cannot deal well with a food or medicine, and not being able to bear heat, cold or pain.
fact: «Lactose intolerance» means the body cannot digest milk sugar well.
fact: An enzyme is a helper substance the body makes to break food apart.
fact: The correct phrase is «zero tolerance», not zero intolerance.
exercise: «Lactose intolerance means the body cannot digest milk sugar well.» In this sentence, what does intolerance mean? | Being very brave | Not being able to bear pain | *The body cannot deal well with a certain food | Not accepting people who are different
exercise: Lessons explain «religious intolerance» and why it hurts people. What does intolerance mean here? | *Not being willing to accept people whose beliefs are different | Needing a lot of sleep | Being unable to bear heat | Food that makes you feel unwell
exercise: «She had an intolerance of cold, so she wore three jumpers.» What does intolerance mean here? | Liking cold weather | *Not being able to bear cold | A medicine for coughs | Being willing to share
test: Which phrase is correct for a firm rule against all unkindness? | zero intolerance | lactose tolerance | *zero tolerance | intolerance of rules
test: Which word means the opposite of tolerance? | enzyme | patience | *intolerance | respect
exam: «Religious intolerance hurts people, so schools teach respect.» Which meaning of intolerance fits? | *Not being willing to accept people whose beliefs are different | The body cannot digest a food well | A helper substance that breaks food apart | Not being able to bear pain
